riginal_operative_text":"Sec. 3. Certain Executive, Legislative, and Judicial Salaries. The rates of \nbasic pay or salaries for the following offices and positions are set forth \non the schedules attached hereto and made a part hereof:","original_source":{"page_or_item":"90 FR 60521, PDF pages 1-15; Sec. 3 (lead-in)","sha256":"11566b889ca3cd4cc48394d9462b1f22b0f3e12a58d335434fbfe4c06e2f35cf","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2025-12-23/pdf/2025-23844.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14368#sec3","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) The Executive Schedule (5 U.S.C. 5311–5318) at Schedule 5;","original_source":{"page_or_item":"90 FR 60521, PDF pages 1-15; Sec. 3(a)","sha256":"11566b889ca3cd4cc48394d9462b1f22b0f3e12a58d335434fbfe4c06e2f35cf","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2025-12-23/pdf/2025-23844.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14368#sec3(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) The Vice President (3 U.S.C. 104) and the Congress (2 U.S.C. 4501) \nat Schedule 6; and","original_source":{"page_or_item":"90 FR 60521, PDF pages 1-15; Sec. 3(b)","sha256":"11566b889ca3cd4cc48394d9462b1f22b0f3e12a58d335434fbfe4c06e2f35cf","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2025-12-23/pdf/2025-23844.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14368#sec3(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(c) Justices and judges (28 U.S.C. 5, 44(d), 135, 252, and 461(a)) at Schedule \n7.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"90 FR 60521, PDF pages 1-15; Sec. 3(c)","sha256":"11566b889ca3cd4cc48394d9462b1f22b0f3e12a58d335434fbfe4c06e2f35cf","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2025-12-23/pdf/2025-23844.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14368#sec3(c)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 4. Uniformed Services and Other. The rates of monthly basic pay \n(37 U.S.C. 203(a)) for members of the uniformed services, as adjusted under \n37 U.S.C. 1009, and the rate of monthly cadet or midshipman pay (37 \nU.S.C. 203(c)) are set forth on Schedule 8 attached hereto and made a \npart hereof. Additionally, the Director of the Office of Personnel Management \n(Director) is directed to assess whether to provide up to a total increase \nof 3.8 percent (inclusive of the increase provided under Section 1) to the \nrates of pay of certain Federal civilian law enforcement personnel, as deter-\nmined by the Director following coordination with agencies and consistent \nwith 5 U.S.C. 5305.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"90 FR 60521, PDF pages 1-15; Sec. 4","sha256":"11566b889ca3cd4cc48394d9462b1f22b0f3e12a58d335434fbfe4c06e2f35cf","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2025-12-23/pdf/2025-23844.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14368#sec4","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) Pursuant to section 5304 \nof title 5, United States Code, and my authority to implement an alternative \nlevel of comparability payments under section 5304a of title 5, United States \nCode, locality-based comparability payments shall be paid in accordance \nwith Schedule 9 attached hereto and made a part hereof.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"90 FR 60521, PDF pages 1-15; Sec. 5(a)","sha256":"11566b889ca3cd4cc48394d9462b1f22b0f3e12a58d335434fbfe4c06e2f35cf","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2025-12-23/pdf/2025-23844.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14368#sec5(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) The Director shall take such actions as may be necessary to implement \nthese payments and to publish appropriate notice of such payments in \nthe Federal Register.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"90 FR 60521, PDF pages 1-15; Sec. 5(b)","sha256":"11566b889ca3cd4cc48394d9462b1f22b0f3e12a58d335434fbfe4c06e2f35cf","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2025-12-23/pdf/2025-23844.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14368#sec5(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 6. Administrative Law Judges. Pursuant to section 5372 of title 5, \nUnited States Code, the rates of basic pay for administrative law judges \nare set forth on Schedule 10 attached hereto and made a part hereof.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"90 FR 60521, PDF pages 1-15; Sec. 6","sha256":"11566b889ca3cd4cc48394d9462b1f22b0f3e12a58d335434fbfe4c06e2f35cf","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2025-12-23/pdf/2025-23844.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14368#sec6","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 7. Effective Dates. Schedule 8 is effective January 1, 2026. The other \nschedules contained herein are effective on the first day of the first applicable \npay period beginning on or after January 1, 2026. \nVerDate Sep<11>2014 19:33 Dec 22, 2025 Jkt 268001 PO 00000 Frm 00003 Fmt 4705 Sfmt 4790 E:\\FR\\FM\\23DEE0.SGM 23DEE0khammond on DSK9W7S144PROD with PRESDOC\n=== PDF page 2 of 15 ===\n60522 Federal Register / Vol. 90, No. 244 / Tuesday, December 23, 2025 / Presidential Documents \nSec. 8. Prior Order Superseded. Executive Order 14132 of December 23, \n2024 (Adjustments of Certain Rates of Pay), is superseded as of the effective \ndates specified in section 7 of this order.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"90 FR 60521, PDF pages 1-15; Sec. 7","sha256":"11566b889ca3cd4cc48394d9462b1f22b0f3e12a58d335434fbfe4c06e2f35cf","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2025-12-23/pdf/2025-23844.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:14368#sec7","state_at_cutoff":null}],"original_representation":{"page_or_item":"90 FR 60521, PDF pages 1-15","sha256":"11566b889ca3cd4cc48394d9462b1f22b0f3e12a58d335434fbfe4c06e2f35cf","url":"https://www.govinfo.go